title: Denial Intelligence › Written appeal › After filing
route: /denials?id=D-3318
intro: A filed appeal (new, or seeded like D-3279, D-3284 and D-3272) shows a waiting block, a read-only letter and the button 'Record the payer's decision'. The payer's answer is recorded by a person, in its own diagram.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the 30-day decision date is fixed, the receipt is saved at filing, and fast-forwarding changes nothing on a filed appeal. Nobody plays the payer, so the person records its decision. In production Navigator finds the answer in its daily check.
---
start s1 "A filed appeal is on screen (after 'Sign and file', or a seeded one)"
screen b1 "Next-step block 'Appeal filed. Waiting on the payer'\n'Filed 10/20, decision 11/19. Navigator checks every day. When the payer answers, record the decision here.'"
screen b2 "Buttons 'View the appeal' and 'Record the payer's decision'\nOther chips: 'Second-level appeal filed', 'External review'\nSeeded appeals read 'Filed 10/05, decision 11/02'"
screen h1 "Header pill 'Appeal filed, decision 11/19'\nList pill 'Decision 11/19'\nNo count-down: the payer has the clock"
process p0 "'Your options' card is hidden"

click c1 "Click 'View the appeal'"
overlay o1 "Drawer 'Appeal letter · D-3318' (read only)\n'Filed by Medical director. Decision 11/19.'\nSeeded appeals read 'Filed 10/05. Decision 11/02.'"
doc dc1 "Letter as filed\n'This is the letter that was filed.'\nEvidence list with greyed tick boxes"
click c2 "Click 'Close', the X, press Esc, or click the dimmed area"

wait w1 "Decision clock runs: 30 days from filing\n(PRD: from confirmed receipt; 72 hours when expedited)"
wait w2 "Navigator checks for the decision each day\nShown in History as a scheduled step"
ext x1 "PRD: receipt call 3 business days after sending\n'Not on file' means resend or a dispute file (not in the demo)"
process p1 "Fast-forward moves the clock, but no status, pill or notification changes on its own"
ext x2 "Payer decides: overturns, partly overturns or upholds\n(demo: nobody plays this)"
click c3 "Click 'Record the payer's decision'"
end e3 "Back on the page, nothing changed"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Request drawer › Check now, Open case and closing"
goto g2 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Written appeal › Record the payer's decision"

s1 --> b1 --> h1
b1 --> p0
b1 --> b2
b2 --> c1 --> o1 --> dc1 --> c2 --> e3
b1 --> w1 --> w2 --> x2
w2 --> x1
w2 -.-> p1
x2 --> c3
b2 --> c3 --> g2
h1 --> g1
